<title>USA: United Carolina Bancshares Q1 net increases.</title>
<headline>United Carolina Bancshares Q1 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>WHITEVILLE, N.C. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended March 31,</p>
<p>						 1997	 1996   % Chg.</p>
<p>  Net interest income		  47,002	42,794     9.8</p>
<p>  Provision for credit losses     (3,850)     (2,200)    75.0</p>
<p>  Net income			     13,279	10,553  25.8 %</p>
<p>Per common share:</p>
<p>    Net income				.55	   .44  25.0 %</p>
<p>    Cash dividends declared	     .18	   .18     - %</p>
<p>Average number of common shares</p>
<p>   outstanding		     24,360,323  24,140,761   0.9 %</p>
<p>	    (Dollars in thousands except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Net income for the fist quarter of 1996 includes the effect of nonrecurring charges and expenses totaling $1.55 million, or $0.06 per share, net of applicable income tax benefits, incurred in connection with the company's mergers with Seaboard Savings Bank and Triad Bank which were consummated during the first quarter of 1996.</p>
</text>
